diff --git a/README.md b/README.md
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..236e171
--- /dev/null
+++ b/README.md
@@ -0,0 +1,54 @@
+# Helpdesk API
+
+Rails 8 API-only backend for account-scoped helpdesk users. PostgreSQL is configured exclusively from `DATABASE_URL`.
+
+## Configuration
+
+- `DATABASE_URL`: PostgreSQL connection URL (required).
+- `HELPDESK_FRONTEND_URL`: frontend base URL; defaults to `http://localhost:3001`.
+- `HELPDESK_MAIL_FROM`: mail sender; defaults to `support@example.test`.
+- `HELPDESK_SUPPORT_DOMAIN`: domain for account and ticket mailboxes; defaults to `support.example.test`.
+- `RAILS_INBOUND_EMAIL_PASSWORD`: password for the Action Mailbox relay ingress (HTTP Basic username `actionmailbox`).
+
+Run `bundle install`, `bin/rails db:prepare`, and `bin/rails server` to start the API. Configure the mail relay to POST RFC 822 messages to `/rails/action_mailbox/relay/inbound_emails` with HTTP Basic credentials. Inbound message bodies are stored through Active Storage; the default configuration uses local disk storage.
+
+All endpoints are available under `/api/v1` and unprefixed compatibility paths. JSON clients select an account with `X-Helpdesk-Account: SUBDOMAIN`. Authenticated requests send `Authorization: Bearer TOKEN`.
+
+Core endpoints:
+
+- `POST /api/v1/account/create`
+- `GET /api/v1/portal`
+- `POST /api/v1/registrations`
+- `GET /api/v1/account`
+- `POST /api/v1/sessions` and `DELETE /api/v1/session`
+- `GET /api/v1/me`, `PATCH /api/v1/me`, and `PUT /api/v1/me/password`
+- `POST /api/v1/email_verifications` and `POST /api/v1/email_verifications/confirm`
+- `POST /api/v1/password_resets` and `POST /api/v1/password_resets/confirm`
+- `POST /api/v1/account/cancel` and `POST /api/v1/account/reactivate`
+- `GET /api/v1/requests`, `POST /api/v1/requests`, `GET|PATCH /api/v1/requests/:id`, and `GET /api/v1/requests/:id/comments`
+- `GET /api/v1/tickets`, `GET|PATCH /api/v1/tickets/:id`, `GET /api/v1/tickets/:id/comments`, and `POST /api/v1/tickets/:id/merge`
+- `GET|POST /api/v1/invitations`, `GET /api/v1/invitations/:id`, `POST /api/v1/invitations/:id/resend`, and `DELETE /api/v1/invitations/:id`
+- `POST /invitation_previews` and `POST /api/v1/invitation_acceptances`
+- `GET /api/v1/users`, `GET|PATCH /api/v1/users/:id`, and `GET /api/v1/staff`
+- `GET|POST /api/v1/groups` and `GET|PATCH|DELETE /api/v1/groups/:id`
+- `GET|POST /api/v1/group_memberships`, `GET|DELETE /api/v1/group_memberships/:id`, and `PUT /api/v1/group_memberships/:id/make_default`
+
+Customers register in a portal, verify their email, and use the same session and recovery endpoints as staff. Admins can invite verified staff as admins or agents. Invitation links point to the frontend acceptance screen and remain valid for seven days. Invitation previews and acceptance require only the unguessable token; acceptance creates an already-verified user.
+
+Incoming plain-text mail to `SUBDOMAIN@HELPDESK_SUPPORT_DOMAIN` opens a ticket for that business; account recipients in `Cc` are recognized too. A known customer is reused, while a new sender gets an unverified customer account and verification email. Automated/list mail, ambiguous multi-business deliveries, and duplicate Message-IDs are ignored.
+
+Every ticket has a private support-domain reply address. Replies from the requester reopen pending or solved email tickets, while mail to the plain business address always opens a new ticket. Replies to closed tickets are ignored. Staff public replies to email-origin tickets are emailed to the requester with the private address as `Reply-To`; private notes and portal-origin tickets remain in-app only.
+
+All collection endpoints support cursor pagination with `page[size]` and `page[after]` or `page[before]`. Cursor responses retain the collection key and add `meta` (`has_more`, `after_cursor`, and `before_cursor`) plus `links.next` and `links.prev`; follow the links or reuse a cursor with the desired page size. `has_more` refers to the direction being browsed. Cursors are opaque and hold a stable ordering boundary while a client traverses a list. The existing `page` and `per_page` page-number parameters and pagination fields remain available.
+
+Request and ticket lists use newest account activity first. Customers can filter their requests by `status`. Staff can combine `status`, `assignee_id`, `requester_id`, `priority`, and literal, case-insensitive `q` search across subjects and public comments. Use `assignee_id=unassigned` for tickets without an assignee. Comment lists are oldest first. Staff may add public comments or private notes, assign tickets to active staff members, and set their priority to `normal` or `high`. Priority defaults to `normal` and is only exposed on staff ticket responses. Assignment, priority-only, and private-note activity do not alter the customer request's activity timestamp.
+
+Admin people lists can filter with `role` and `suspended`; invitation lists can filter with `status`. People and invitation lists use ascending IDs, as do active staff choices. Suspending a staff member revokes their sessions and clears their ticket assignments. The last active admin cannot be suspended.
+
+Staff can browse all groups and group memberships; only admins may change them. Group and membership lists use ascending IDs, and membership lists can filter by `group_id` and `user_id`. A staff member can belong to multiple groups but always has one default membership while any memberships remain. Suspending staff preserves those memberships for later reactivation.
+
+Staff can merge duplicate tickets for the same customer with `POST /api/v1/tickets/:id/merge` and a `merge.target_id`. The source is closed, unassigned, and retains its original comments and `merged_into_id` link while the target's status, assignment, and email identity are unchanged. A merge adds a private source note and target note by default; `source_comment` and `target_comment` may each override `body` and `public`. Merge notes never send email. Closed tickets remain readable and appear in `status=closed` staff and customer lists, but cannot be edited or reopened by further replies. Later merges preserve existing merge links.
+
+Staff ticket responses include `group_id` and a `group` object containing the group ID and name. Ticket lists can filter with `group_id`, including `group_id=unassigned`. Assigning someone to an ungrouped ticket uses the assignee's default group when available; assignments are cleared when a group change or group/membership deletion makes them invalid. Clearing only an assignee preserves the group, while clearing the group also clears the assignee.
+
+Cancelled accounts are blocked from ordinary access, revoke all sessions, and may be reactivated by their owner for 90 days. Run `bin/rails helpdesk:purge_cancelled_accounts` to permanently remove accounts past that window and cascade their data deletion.
